title: '[RESIDUAL] shared relay fixture parity gaps and optional nightly real-relay coverage'
---
Most of this idea shipped through the shared relay test-support work.

`Relay_test_support` is the single scripted loopback HTTP fault harness. It supports arbitrary 401/429/5xx responses, sequenced responses, slow/timeouts, truncated bodies, malformed JSON, connection refusal, close-without-response, request capture, and schema mismatch. It deliberately contains no registration, inbox, room, or PoW semantics.

`Relay_test_support_real` mounts the production `Relay_server(InMemoryRelay)` handler for real register/PoW, DM send/poll, list/status, room, auth, and persistence-independent semantics. Do not replace this split with a second stateful fake relay.

Existing regressions cover B087 null/missing/wrong-type PoW parsing, B088 queued remote-send reporting, B098 inert-message and process-level relay-to-inbox approval isolation, B090's now-obsolete HTTPS rejection path, and broad 401/429/5xx, timeout, truncation, malformed-JSON, and schema-mismatch matrices.

Residual work, if still valuable, is narrow:

1. Add relay-room operations to the scripted/real equality vector; it currently covers register, send, poll, health, and list.
2. Add one exact process-level `required:null` PoW response -> `relay connect --once` nonzero regression; exact-null coverage currently stops at the connector parser.
3. Decide whether a scheduled public-relay smoke workflow belongs in CI. Hermetic fixtures exist; no nightly public-relay workflow was found.
